# Shell and Python scripts must check out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites these to CRLF on checkout.
# bash then fails on the trailing carriage return with `$'\r': command not found`, and
# because .githooks/pre-commit runs the contract gate, a Windows contributor's very first
# commit breaks with an error that reads like a corrupt repo rather than a line-ending
# setting. The pack's audit scripts fail the same way in a consuming project.
#
# core.autocrlf is per-machine and cannot be committed; this can.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf

# Extensionless executables, matched by name since no glob covers them.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
